{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this file to `.mcp.json` in the ROOT OF THE REPO YOU WANT TO TRACK",
    "(not in the evalharness folder), then replace the two placeholders below.",
    "Delete this _comment key if your agent is strict about unknown fields.",
    "",
    "  <ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_EVALHARNESS>  the folder you cloned this repo into,",
    "                                  e.g. /home/you/tools/evalharness",
    "  <ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_YOUR_REPO>    the repo whose work you want to capture,",
    "                                  e.g. /home/you/work/my-rtl-project",
    "",
    "Both must be ABSOLUTE paths — the agent launches the server with an",
    "unpredictable working directory. EVALHARNESS_REPO is what tells the server",
    "which repo's .evalharness/ directory to read and write.",
    "",
    "The optional env vars below can be deleted if you don't use them:",
    "  CVDP_DATASET            default path for `import_cvdp` (you supply this file)",
    "  CVDP_BASELINE_MANIFEST  default path for `import_baseline` FINAL_MANIFEST.json",
    "  EVALHARNESS_PET_NAME    rename the persona (default: EvalScout)",
    "  EVALHARNESS_PET_ICON    change the persona icon (default: [*_*] style face)"
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "evalharness": {
      "command": "python3",
      "args": [
        "<ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_EVALHARNESS>/mcp_server.py"
      ],
      "env": {
        "EVALHARNESS_REPO": "<ABSOLUTE_PATH_TO_YOUR_REPO>",
        "CVDP_DATASET": "",
        "CVDP_BASELINE_MANIFEST": "",
        "EVALHARNESS_PET_NAME": "EvalScout"
      }
    }
  }
}
